 				Records a call to [param callback] into the render graph at the current position. When the graph is recorded into the native command buffer, [param callback] is called once with that command buffer's native handle (see [constant DRIVER_RESOURCE_COMMAND_BUFFER]) so native SDKs (DLSS, FidelityFX, XeSS) can record their own commands into the frame. [param resources] lists the textures / buffers the callback touches, with one [enum CallbackResourceType] and one [enum CallbackResourceUsage] each; the graph transitions them before the call, and the call is ordered only against these declared resources (with render-graph reordering an undeclared dependency may run out of order). Vulkan only: other drivers return [constant ERR_UNAVAILABLE]. The callback runs on the rendering thread during submission and must not call [RenderingDevice] methods. Must be called on the rendering thread outside of draw, compute and raytracing lists.
 			</description>
 		</method>
